    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe API now returns a `timezone` field on owners, derived from the region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **`Localities.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` map and a new one-line `timezoneFor(region)` method (cyclomatic complexity 1) to the small util class that already owns the region tables \u2014 its natural, cohesive home.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` line for `timezone` that composes `Localities.timezoneFor(...)` with the existing `CustomerCodes.regionOf(...)` used for `locality`. No existing method body was touched, so no complex method grew.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `timezone` schema field so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite are green.",
